  "status": "rebranded",
  "activeSince": "2020",
  "lineage": "Shut down May 2021 after Colonial Pipeline; rebranded as BlackMatter (Jul 2021), whose operators are linked to ALPHV/BlackCat",
  "summary": "DarkSide was a RaaS active from August 2020 that became infamous for the May 2021 Colonial Pipeline attack. Mandiant tracked several affiliate clusters: UNC2465 (phishing with the SMOKEDHAM backdoor and NGROK), UNC2628 (VPN password spraying, Cobalt Strike), and UNC2659 (SonicWall SMA100 CVE-2021-20016, TeamViewer). Operators used RDP, Tor and Cobalt Strike, exfiltrated with Rclone/MEGA, and shipped both Windows and Linux/ESXi encryptors.",
  "uniqueTraits": [
    "UNC2659 exploited SonicWall SMA100 SSL-VPN CVE-2021-20016",
    "UNC2465 used SMOKEDHAM .NET backdoor and NGROK tunnels to expose RDP",
    "Linux/ESXi encryptor that enumerates and targets VMware virtual machines",
    "Tor multi-hop proxying for C2 and leak site"
  ],
  "insufficientReporting": false,
